    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="32">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 32</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.1"/><pb n="514" ed="#liebermann"/>Nullui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.2"/> ne toille a soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.3"/> seinour<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.4"/> sun dreit servise pur nul relais, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.5"/> il li ait fait en arere.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="514" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne quis iustum seruicium domino subtrahat. Nullus pro quacumque remissione ei a domino gratuito facta debitum subtrahat servicium.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="32" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="268" ed="#robertson"/>Nullui ne toille a soun seinour sun dreit servise pur nul relais que il li ait fait en arere.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="514" ed="#liebermann"/>32. Keiner entziehe seinem Herrn seinen richtigen Dienst wegen eines Erlasses<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_32.lnote.de.1"/>, den ihm dieser früher gewährt haben mag.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">32. Let no one withhold from his lord his proper service on account of a remission which the latter may formerly have granted him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="269" ed="#robertson"/>No-one shall withdraw his legal service from his lord on account of any remission which had been granted to him in the past.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 268–269 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 514, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">514</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXXIIII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXXIIII. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">514</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nului <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Nului Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">514</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">514</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">senior <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">senior Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">514</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_32.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">291</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">An Fron und Zins; nicht, wie Kelham meint, Aufschub in Zurückforderung des entlaufenen Bauern; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 10c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Of labour services and rent; not, as Kelham thinks, a respite in reclaiming the runaway peasant; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 10c</seg></note>
      </div>
